Subject: [PATCH] sycl: fold the residual / bias ADD after a one-column mat-vec into the DMMV store

Local port of the MUL_MAT + ADD fusion CUDA, Vulkan and Metal run on the residual add after the attention
output and the FFN down projection (and on biases). ggml_sycl_mul_mat_add_fused points the mat-vec at the
ADD's memory and hands the addend through the context; the DMMV kernels add it in their store:
the ESIMD reorder kernels the A770 runs for q2_K..q6_K and q8_0 (a separate policy, since IGC's ESIMD back
end crashes on a load behind a run-time null check), and the generic plain / reorder kernels (q4_0, q4_1,
q5_0, q5_1, q8_0, q1_0). A kernel that does not take it (MMVQ, the non-ESIMD k-quant DMMV) leaves its
plain result there and one in-place ADD follows, so the fusion never adds a launch. Overlaps of the
ADD's memory with the activation or the addend decline; graph_optimize keeps the activation alive until
the ADD so the allocator does not produce the first.

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp
index 15f71809..289f91e9 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp
@@ -602,6 +602,12 @@ struct ggml_backend_sycl_context {
 
     queue_ptr qptrs[GGML_SYCL_MAX_DEVICES][GGML_SYCL_MAX_STREAMS] = { { nullptr } };
 
+    // MUL_MAT + ADD fusion (ggml_sycl_mul_mat_add_fused): the addend of the ADD after a one-column mat-vec
+    // whose output the mat-vec writes. A DMMV kernel that folds it into its store writes sum + mmv_add[row] and
+    // sets mmv_add_applied; otherwise the caller runs the ADD.
+    const float * mmv_add         = nullptr;
+    bool          mmv_add_applied = false;
+
     explicit ggml_backend_sycl_context(int device) :
         device(device),
         name(GGML_SYCL_NAME + std::to_string(device)) {
